1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:07,536
AI agents now pay for APIs and sign transactions on their own. One wrong signature can empty a wallet.

2
00:00:08,001 --> 00:00:13,313
So we built two checks for the two risky moments: before an agent pays, and before it signs.

3
00:00:14,574 --> 00:00:21,635
x402 Doctor checks a paid API the way a paying agent would. Here it diagnoses a broken one.

4
00:00:22,094 --> 00:00:26,915
Every problem, with the reason and the fix. For developers the web check is free.

5
00:00:27,383 --> 00:00:37,559
For agents there's x402-safe-fetch. Before it pays an unknown API, it buys a Doctor preflight for a tenth of a cent. No-go means no payment.

6
00:00:38,023 --> 00:00:43,271
And when a payment still fails, it buys one diagnosis for a cent that says exactly why.

7
00:00:45,174 --> 00:00:51,126
The second check is presign-guard. It answers one question before an agent signs: is this safe?

8
00:00:52,196 --> 00:01:01,753
presign-guard-wallet wraps the agent's wallet. Every transaction and signature is checked first. Green signs, orange asks, and red is never signed.

9
00:01:02,218 --> 00:01:12,543
Every verdict is cryptographically signed, and both packages check that signature. A forged green is never a payment or a signature. Your keys stay in your own code.

10
00:01:18,184 --> 00:01:22,856
And it's all live: every call to the services, on lab.fizzl.eu.

11
00:01:28,039 --> 00:01:37,063
Install presign-guard-wallet and x402-safe-fetch from npm, or try the free checks on the web. Safe money for AI agents.

